for key,m in media.items():supp+=p('<a href="'+m['source_url']+'">'+html.escape(m['title'])+'</a> — '+html.escape(m['mime_type']))
supp+=p('All eleven public media URLs returned HTTP 200. The five GIFs were downloaded from those public URLs and independently read with the system ImageIO decoder: each retains all 65 frames at 1100×720 pixels. Static PNG fallbacks are available for reduced-motion reading. The animations use representative seed 17, shared force/geometry scales and explicit boundary labels; five-seed variability appears in the main chart and complete data.')
supp+=h('Execution audit')+code((root/'data/audit.json').read_text())
supp+=markdown((root/'METHODS.md').read_text())+markdown((root/'EVIDENCE.md').read_text())
supp+=h('Source inspection and execution boundary')+p('Existing collagen explorer code and the prior archive were read as untrusted context and not executed. The new solver, tests, UI, benchmark and rendering code are original. Node standard library and native macOS drawing frameworks were used; no new dependency, remote solver or molecular workload was installed or run. The package contains SECURITY-REVIEW.md with the bounded inspection scope and residual risks. Publishing did not send subscriber email or request social sharing.')
